@startuml
title AnonyIG - Technical Architecture (Sequence)

actor Visitor as User
participant "Vue SPA\n(anonyig.com)" as FE
participant "Query Parser\n+ Search Controller" as Ctrl
participant "Signer Chunk\n(link.chunk.js)" as Signer
participant "Turnstile / Token Store" as Gate
participant "Worker Hub API\napi-wh.anonyig.com" as Hub
participant "Scraper Orchestrator" as Orch
participant "Session Pool" as Sessions
participant "Residential Proxy Pool" as Proxies
participant "Instagram\nWeb/Mobile Surfaces" as IG
participant "Media Proxy CDN\nmedia.anonyig.com" as Media

User -> FE : Enter @username or Instagram URL
FE -> Ctrl : onSearch / submit
Ctrl -> Ctrl : Classify query\n(userInfo / stories / posts / convert)
Ctrl -> Signer : Build request envelope
Signer -> Signer : Compute ts + signature _s
Signer --> Ctrl : Signed payload
Ctrl -> Gate : Attach x-token / wh-cf-token
Gate -> Hub : POST /api/v2/instagram/{resource}

alt Abuse signal 422 or 429
  Hub --> FE : Captcha required
  FE -> Gate : Complete Cloudflare Turnstile
  Gate -> Hub : Retry with fresh wh-cf-token
end

Hub -> Orch : Validate signature and dispatch
Orch -> Sessions : Acquire session if required
Orch -> Proxies : Rotate residential IP
Proxies -> IG : Fetch profile / stories / posts JSON
IG --> Proxies : Raw Instagram payload
Proxies --> Orch : Relay
Orch -> Orch : Normalize to client schema
Orch -> Media : Rewrite media URLs
Hub --> Ctrl : Normalized JSON
Ctrl --> User : Render profile, stories, posts, downloads

note right of Hub
  Browser never scrapes Instagram directly.
  Worker Hub does acquisition server-side.
end note

@enduml
